{"boundary":"Configured source-text signatures, not elaborated Lean or a complete dependency context. Truncation and unresolved names are explicit; full definitions and source remain on demand.","contributions":[{"author":{"kind":"agent","name":"Codex source review 2"},"body":"Source reading supports the stated bounded navigation relation; this is agent-authored and unreviewed.\n\nInspected: Read finite-machine transition/halting definitions, effective-family and real-oracle evaluation contracts, PDE, comparison class, compact support, fixed observer and full endpoint.","content_sha256":"sha256:413b841be0cd600c283aa42c2e03e5192bf367b19c8180bc634a31a2169fc6fd","fingerprint":"sha256:76a2bceb70606d374ae9907078a5972289ffeb716e61bea7325e7b802a1bf788","kind":"statement-link","license":"Apache-2.0","navigation":{"decision":"linked","limitations":"Agent source reading; no human approval, Lean replay or whole-statement equivalence certificate. Source reading supports the stated bounded navigation relation; this is agent-authored and unreviewed.","schema":"statement-map-navigation-reading/1","source_sha256":"sha256:dd177cc30a8ed9a0012d32b8ab6900681c7ec6089dc121e592883162a08f2d76","targets":[{"declarations":["OAI.BalancedTransport.balanced_three_stack_realization"],"explanation":"The configured theorem supplies effective viscosity-independent coefficients f0 and f1 and a zero-data velocity on R3 with compact spatial support, bounded mixed derivatives and period one after time one. The material particle from (4,0,0) enters (-1,2)^3 exactly when the encoded machine halts; the repeated velocity depends on the machine but not its input. Its affine force f0+nu*f1, positive-real viscosity quantifier, relative evaluation and pressure-modulo-constants comparison class match the balanced-three-stack theorem.","fingerprint":"sha256:b7a2ae5cee749c3e76e2fb806fda61acf68520b0b3dd1ade54a60e23dbaa21b0","limitations":"This is the Euclidean periodic-after-one construction, not the torus stationary-forcing result or a generic assertion about all Navier-Stokes solutions.","relation":"same-claim","row_id":"Incompressible-Box-Transport-and-Finite-Computation-October-6-2026#thm:bb-balanced-three-stack","statement_sha256":"sha256:8a239e2b040c28f760774c24cbc405abdc094d7fc67bea543c7df8e72a2d3a8d"}]},"pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","provenance":{"identity_assurance":"named local attestation; identity not independently authenticated","kind":"agent-drafted-unreviewed"},"references":["https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/lean/ComparatorChallenges/ForcedNavierStokesComputation.lean","https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Incompressible-Box-Transport-and-Finite-Computation-October-6-2026/build/balanced.tex#L11"],"release_id":"openai-math","review_state":"unreviewed","row_id":"challenge:ForcedNavierStokesComputation","schema":"statement-map-contribution/1"}],"detail":{"path":"lean/1cf5a07a6ad3ac7971283e78.json","pointer":""},"formal_statement":{"detail":{"path":"lean/1cf5a07a6ad3ac7971283e78.json","pointer":"/reader/formal_statement"},"full_source":{"path":"lean/1cf5a07a6ad3ac7971283e78.json","pointer":"/reader/formal_statement"},"kind":"declaration-signatures","method":"configured-challenge-declaration-signatures","name_resolution":"source-text","snippets":[{"complete":true,"detail":{"path":"lean/1cf5a07a6ad3ac7971283e78.json","pointer":"/reader/selected_statements/0"},"full_source":{"path":"lean/1cf5a07a6ad3ac7971283e78.json","pointer":"/challenge/lean"},"name":"OAI.BalancedTransport.balanced_three_stack_realization","source":{"file":"lean/ComparatorChallenges/ForcedNavierStokesComputation.lean","line":206,"pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","sha256":"dd177cc30a8ed9a0012d32b8ab6900681c7ec6089dc121e592883162a08f2d76","statement_sha256":"sha256:da69b724b49d92e422e4e5fe0460b23c05c22354cce8b3929ab40320f3d3be3d","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/lean/ComparatorChallenges/ForcedNavierStokesComputation.lean#L206"},"text":"theorem balanced_three_stack_realization :\n    ∃ U f₀ f₁ : Family Velocity,\n    ∃ X : Family MaterialFlow,\n    ∃ repeated : FiniteMachine → Velocity,\n      EffectiveFamily U ∧ EffectiveFamily f₀ ∧ EffectiveFamily f₁ ∧\n      (∀ M, Function.Periodic (repeated M) 1) ∧\n      ∀ (M : FiniteMachine) (w : Input M),\n        Smooth (U M w) ∧ Smooth (f₀ M w) ∧ Smooth (f₁ M w) ∧\n        f₀ M w = inertialCoefficient (U M w) ∧\n        f₁ M w = viscousCoefficient (U M w) ∧\n        CommonCompactSupport (U M w) (f₀ M w) (f₁ M w) ∧\n        BoundedMixed (U M w) ∧\n        PeriodicAfterOne (U M w) ∧\n        (∀ t, 1 ≤ t → ∀ x, U M w t x = repeated M t x) ∧\n        ComparisonClass (U M w) (fun _ _ => 0) ∧\n        IsMaterialFlow (U M w) (X M w) ∧\n        ((∃ t : ℝ, 0 ≤ t ∧ X M w t fixedLabel ∈ observer) ↔ Halts M w) ∧\n        ∀ ν : ℝ, 0 < ν →\n          let f := affineForce (f₀ M w) (f₁ M w) ν\n          ZeroDataSolution ν f (U M w) (fun _ _ => 0) ∧\n          Smooth f ∧ BoundedMixed f ∧ PeriodicAfterOne f ∧\n          UniqueInComparison ν f (U M w) ∧\n          (ComputableReal ν → EffectiveFieldIn ∅ f) ∧\n          (∀ name : ℕ → ℚ, RealName name ν → EffectiveFieldIn {nameOracle name} f)"}],"state":"available","unresolved_names":[]},"generation_id":"sha256:c701139844a2d825c371ded7486924e7dae7de0af77a69dc9c1abaf1129191a1","id":"l:ForcedNavierStokesComputation","kind":"lean-preview","omissions":[],"pairings":{"f:376":{"alternatives":["pair:4f7e4233b652a91badb71cf2","pair:92a6fd574fe9d445db984c8f","pair:74f272ac7e70c1a1c7a94dbe","pair:146e2f589550fb14088e2107","pair:67b843c3bab89886c3556472","pair:dc07af2f1544728b648a62a6"],"contributed_readings":[{"author":{"kind":"agent","name":"Codex source review 2"},"content_sha256":"sha256:413b841be0cd600c283aa42c2e03e5192bf367b19c8180bc634a31a2169fc6fd","decision":"linked","detail":{"path":"lean-previews/1cf5a07a6ad3ac797